  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM Shelters: Supporting and Protecting Unaccompanied Migrant Children in Greece</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this Action, IOM seeks to continue operating six (6) Shelters for UMC with a total capacity of up to 152 beds/places in the regions of Attica (four shelters), Central Macedonia (Thessaloniki, one shelter) and Western Greece (Patra, one shelter) from 1 February 2022 to 31 January 2023. One of the shelters in Attica is accommodating girls (Ilion), while all other boys. The six shelters will be operational since the project beginning and until 24 March 2022. As of 25 March 2022, and until 31 January 2023 five (5) shelters with the total capacity of 132 places will continue hosting UMC and being financially supported under the present Action. During their stay in the Shelters, UMC will be provided with dignified accommodation and tailored protection in accordance with their best interests, by experienced IOM staff. To this end, IOM will capitalize on its previous experience in operating UMC Shelters, as well as in providing safe and dignified accommodation to UMC and other migrants in a situation of vulnerability in Greece.</narrative>
  </description>
